  "body": "There is no shipped wire EDM machine file: the Sodick wire post of issue 617 is tested on the synthetic fixture (`crates/app/tests/edm/wire-iso-fixture.mch`). A user with a Sodick wire EDM has to write a machine file by hand before the post can be picked.\n\nWanted: a Sodick wire EDM machine file in `assets/machines/` (kind `wire_edm`, X Y U V travels, guide heights, maximum taper, `edm.awt`, a small set of conditions named as `C` and three digits) taken from Sodick's published specifications for one named model, each number with its public source; numbers that cannot be sourced are left out (the app refuses what needs them) rather than guessed. The file names \"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\" as its post only if the model's control is the one the post was written from.\n\nDone means: the machine file loads, lists the Sodick post in the picker, and a punch posts through it in a test; the file's header names the source of every travel and limit.\n\nPart of #617\n",
